  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening indigenous collective initiatives and electronic workers rights in Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD has contributed financially for more than ten years to Fomento&apos;s projects. Fomento will celebrate its 40th anniversary next August. In the process of phasing out Mexico, this project with Fomento is a phasing out project  to strengthen the areas of Fomento&apos;s work which will stay connected to CAFOD  programmes and advocacy work after funding ends: electronic industry advocacy work and land and territorial rights of Indigenous Peoples in Chiapas. The project will also strengthen the administrative and institutional development areas of Fomento in search of new funding oportunities.

The aim of the Project is to strengthen Indigenous communities in Chiapas and electronic industry workers in Mexico to live with dignity building a just, democratic and multicultural nation in harmony with nature.</narrative>
  </description>
